EXT. CANAL LOCK - ABANDONED BARGE - DUSK

Mud. Reeds. A gutted barge half sunk in the lock chamber. Rain thinning to nothing.

SERGEANT KOWALCZYK, 30s, ash-faced, crouches on the deck. Rifle across his knees. He counts rounds by touch.

PRIVATE TEMBO, 19, scrawny, huddles behind a coil of rope. Helmet too big. Shaking.

CORPORAL ISHIDA, 20s, steady, sweeps the far bank through a cracked scope.

Silence. Distant guns, getting farther.

TEMBO
Is that it? Are they gone?

KOWALCZYK
Shut up and breathe.

ISHIDA
Nothing moving. Tree line's clear.

Kowalczyk looks at the hatch. A knock from below. Three slow raps.

All three men freeze. Rifles up.

KOWALCZYK
Hands. Now.

The hatch lifts a few inches. A woman's hand. Then a face. A CIVILIAN WOMAN, 30s, soaked, coat buttoned wrong, clutches a canvas bag to her chest.

CIVILIAN WOMAN
Don't shoot. Please.

ISHIDA
Who are you?

CIVILIAN WOMAN
I live here. I live on the barge.

TEMBO
Nobody lives here.

CIVILIAN WOMAN
I do.

Kowalczyk lowers the rifle an inch. Doesn't lower it more.

KOWALCZYK
Name.

CIVILIAN WOMAN
Mireille.

KOWALCZYK
Anyone else down there, Mireille?

MIREILLE
A cat.

Tembo laughs. Short. Cracked. Then it turns into something else and he presses his sleeve to his mouth.

Ishida hands him a canteen. Doesn't say anything.

KOWALCZYK
You hungry?

MIREILLE
Yes.

Kowalczyk digs in his pack. Tosses a tin. She catches it with one hand, bag still clamped under the other arm.

MIREILLE (CONT'D)
They'll come back at dawn.

ISHIDA
We know.

MIREILLE
There's a way out. Under the sluice gate.

Kowalczyk studies her. Rain starts again, light.

KOWALCZYK
Show us.
